cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PHI-Weaver, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PHI-Weaver: AI-assisted ontology-based curation and term suggestion for pathogen-host interactions"
abstract: >-
  A curator-in-the-loop framework that assists PHI-base and PHI-Canto curation
  workflows using large language models. Covers literature intake, ontology term
  lookup and validation (PHIPO, PHIDO, PECO, GO), annotation drafting against
  documented curation standards, and quality checks.
license: MIT  # software; repository content is CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-CONTENT)
repository-code: "https://github.com/PHI-base/phi-weaver"
url: "https://github.com/PHI-base/phi-weaver"
keywords:
  - biocuration
  - pathogen-host interactions
  - PHI-base
  - PHI-Canto
  - PHIPO
  - ontology annotation
  - large language models
authors:
  # Co-author list still to confirm. Two conditions must both hold before adding
  # someone: an intellectual contribution to the work, AND their agreement to be
  # listed (their name on a curation tool implies they stand behind its output).
  # Candidates: Hsin-Yu Chang (curation standards, validation authority),
  # James Seager (software), Alayne Cuzick. Until each says yes, credit belongs
  # in the README Acknowledgments section, not here. ORCIDs are optional.
  - family-names: Urban
    given-names: Martin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2440-4352"
    affiliation: Rothamsted Research

# Deliberately omitted, to avoid asserting something that is not yet true:
#   version:         - would need updating at every release
#   date-released:   - ditto
#   doi:             - add the Zenodo *concept* DOI once a release is minted
#   preferred-citation: - add if a PHI-Weaver paper is published, so citations
#                         point at the article rather than at this repository
